# Degree, Cardinality and Optionality
Note: M – Mandatory, O – Optional

1)	Boss is summoned by Item (1:1, O-O)  
— A boss is summoned by one item;  
— An item summons one boss;  
— Not every boss can be summoned by an item;  
— Not every item summons a boss.  

2)	Boss drops Item (N:M, O-O)  
— A boss drops many items;  
— An item is dropped by many bosses;  
— Not every boss drops an item;  
— Not every item is dropped by a boss.  

3)	Boss has Boss Part (1:N, O-M)  
— A boss has many parts;  
— A boss part belongs to one boss;  
— Not every boss has a part;  
— Every boss part belongs to a boss.  

4)	Boss Part Stage spawns Enemy (N:M, O-O)  
— A boss part stage spawns many enemies;  
— An enemy is spawned by many boss part stages;  
— Not every boss part stage spawns an enemy;  
— Not every enemy is spawned by a boss part stage.  

5)	Boss Part is a Entity (1:1, M-O)  
— A boss part is one entity;  
— An entity is one boss part;  
— Every boss part is a entity;  
— Not every entity is a boss part.  

6) Boss Part Stage is a stage of Boss Part (N:1, M-O)  
— A boss part stage is a stage of one boss part;  
— A boss part has many boss part stages;  
— Every boss part stage is a stage of a boss part;  
— Not every boss part has a boss part stage.  

7)	Enemy is a Entity (1:1, M-O)  
— An enemy is one entity;  
— An entity is one enemy;  
— Every enemy is an entity;  
— Not every entity is an enemy.  

8)	Item is dropped by Entity (N:M, O-O)  
— An item is dropped by many entities;  
— An entity drops many items;  
— Not every item is dropped by an entity.  
— Not every entity drops an item;  

9)	Item has Item Form (1:N, O-M)  
— An item has many item forms;  
— An item form belongs to one item;  
— Not every item has an item form.  
— Every item form belongs to an item;  

10)	Item is traded by Town NPC (N:M, O-O)  
— An item is traded by many town NPCs;  
— A town NPC trades many items;  
— Not every item is traded by a town NPC;  
— Not every town NPC trades an item.  

11)	Item is a CraftingStation (N:1, O-O)  
— An item is one crafting station;  
— A crafting station is many items;  
— Not every item is a crafting station;  
— Not every crafting station is an item.  

12)	Town NPC is a Entity (1:1, M-O)  
— A town NPC is one entity;  
— An entity is one town NPC;  
— Every town NPC is an entity;  
— Not every entity is a town NPC.  

13)	Town NPC has Town NPC Form (1:N, O-M)  
— A town NPC has many town NPC forms;  
— A town NPC form belongs to one town NPC;  
— Not every town NPC has a town NPC form;  
— Every town NPC form belongs to a town NPC. 

14)	Item is a result of crafting with Item on Crafting Station (1:N:1, O-O-O)  
—	An item is a result of crafting with an item on one crafting station;  
—	An item is a result of crafting on a crafting station with many items;  
—	A result of crafting with an item on a crafting station is one item;  
— Not every item is a result of crafting;  
— Not every item is required for crafting.  
— Not every crafting station is used for crafting.  

## Table 1 - Relationships between entities
| N | Relationship |	Cardinality | Optionality |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 |	Boss is summoned by Item |	1:1 |	O-O |
| 2 |	Boss drops Item |	N:M	 | O-O |
| 3 |	Boss has Boss Part |	1:N |	O-M |
| 4 |	Boss Part Stage spawns Enemy |	N:M |	O-O |
| 5 |	Boss Part is a Entity |	1:1 |	M-O |
| 6 |	Boss Part Stage is a stage of Boss Part |	N:1 |	M-O |
| 7 |	Enemy is a Entity |	1:1 |	M-O |
| 8 |	Item is dropped by Entity |	N:M |	O-O |
| 9 |	Item has Item Form |	1:N |	O-M |
| 10 |	Item is traded by Town NPC |	N:M |	O-O |
| 11 |	Item is a Crafting Station |	N:1 |	O-O |
| 12 |	Town NPC is a Entity |	1:1 |	M-O |
| 13 |	Town NPC has Town NPC Form |	1:N |	O-M |
| 14 |	Item is a result of crafting with Item on Crafting Station |	1:N:1 |	O-O-O |

