# Candidate keys and attributes of entities
Note: CK – Candidate Key
1)	**Boss** (#BossName)  
— Boss Name (CK);  
— Boss Sprite (CK).
2)	**Boss Part** (BossPartId).  
— Boss Part ID (CK);  
— Boss Part Order ID;  
— Quantity.  
1) **Boss Part Stage** (#BossPartStageId)  
— Boss Part Stage ID (CK);  
— Boss Part Stage Order ID;  
— Sprite;  
— Contact Damage;  
— Hp;  
— Defense.  
4)	**Enemy** (#EnemyId)  
— Enemy ID (CK);  
— Contact Damage;  
— Hp;  
— Defense.  
5)	**Entity** (#InternalNpcId)  
— Internal NPC ID (CK);  
— Entity Name;  
— Description.  
6)	**Town NPC** (#TownNpcId)  
— Town NPC ID (CK);  
— Hp;  
— Defense.  
7)	**Town NPC Form** (#TownNpcFormId)  
— Town NPC Form ID (CK);  
— Town NPC Form Order ID;  
— Town NPC Form Sprite (CK).  
8)	**Item** (#InternalItemId)  
— Internal Item ID (CK);  
— Item Name;  
— Buy Price;  
— Sell Price;  
— Buy Price Currency Type.  
9)	**Item Form** (#ItemFormId)  
— Item Form ID (CK);  
— Item Form Order ID;  
— Item Sprite;  
— Tooltip.  
9)	**Crafting Station** (#CraftingStationName)  
— Crafting Station Name (CK);  
— Crafting Station Sprite (CK);  

# Resolving N-ary relationships
Crafting relationship → Recipe entity:
1)	**Item is used in Recipe** (N:M, O-M)  
— An item is used in many recipes;  
— A recipe requires many items;  
— Not every item is used in a recipe;  
— Every recipe requires an item.  
2)	**Item is a result of Recipe** (1:N, O-M)  
— An item is a result of many recipes;  
— A recipe results in one item;  
— Not every item is a result of a recipe;  
— Every recipe results in an item.  
3)	**Recipe requires Crafting Station** (N:1, O-O)  
— A recipe requires one crafting station;  
— A crafting station is required for many recipes;  
— Not every recipe requires a crafting station;  
— Not every crafting station is required for a recipe.  
Recipe attributes:  
— Recipe ID (CK);  
— ResultItemQuantity.  

# Resolving Many-to-Many relationships
Boss drops Item → BossDrop (BossName, ItemId, Quantity)  
Boss Part Form spawns Enemy → BossPartStageEnemies (BossPartStageId, EnemyId, Quantity)  
Item is traded by Town NPC → TradeOffer (ItemId, TownNpcId, Quantity, TradeType)  
Item is dropped by Entity → EntityDrop (ItemId, EntityId, Quantity)  
Item is used in Recipe → RecipeItems (ItemId, RecipeId, Quantity)  

